# BusinessSuite ERP — Access Control & Design System

## Menu rights model (mandatory for every menu)

Every menu/page must register in `lib/menu-registry.ts` with:
- `id` (stable, e.g. `hrm.employees`)
- `module`, `label`, `href`, `keywords`
- rights: `view` (default gate), `create`, `update`, `delete`

Permissions are assigned at **two levels**:
1. **Role level** — default matrix for a role (e.g. accountant / hr_manager)
2. **User level** — per-user overrides (grant or revoke on top of role)

Effective rights = role rights merged with user overrides (user wins).

Super Admin / Company Admin always have full rights unless explicitly revoked at user level by Super Admin only.

## When adding a new menu

1. Add entry to `lib/menu-registry.ts` (and `navGroups` in `lib/permissions.ts`)
2. Gate the page with `canMenu(user, menuId, "view")`
3. Gate buttons with `canMenu(user, menuId, "create"|"update"|"delete")`
4. Ensure it appears in global top search (automatic via registry)
5. Use shared UI primitives only — never invent ad-hoc input/button/card styles

## Design system (single source of truth)

- Active theme file: `config/theme.json` (updated by admin Access Control)
- Default theme file: `config/theme.default.json` (reset target)
- API: `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/theme`
- CSS variables in `app/globals.css` (`--bs-*`) are applied at runtime from the JSON
- Inputs/Buttons/Cards must use shared UI primitives + CSS vars — never hardcode random colors
- "Reset to default theme" restores `theme.json` from `theme.default.json`

## Global search

Top nav center search must list **all** menus from the registry the current user can `view`. Future menus must be registry-driven so search stays complete. Support autocomplete + ⌘K / Ctrl+K focus. See also `.cursor/rules/erp-nav-ux.mdc` for breadcrumbs and grouped module navigation.
